#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:111
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:113
msgid "`options` The options object passed in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:114
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`interval` {integer} Interval to pass to `fs.watchFile`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:115
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`debounceDelay` {integer} Delay for events called in succession for the "
"same file/event in milliseconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:117
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`mode` {string} Force the watch mode. Either `'auto'` (default), "
"`'watch'` (force native events), or `'poll'` (force stat polling)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:118
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`cwd` {string} The current working directory to base file patterns from. "
"Default is `process.cwd()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:120
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:122
msgid "`ready(watcher)` When files have been globbed and watching has begun."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:123
msgid ""
"`all(event, filepath)` When an `added`, `changed`, `renamed`, or "
"`deleted` event occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:124
msgid "`added(filepath)` When a file has been added to a watch directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:125
msgid "`changed(filepath)` When a file has been changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:126
msgid "`deleted(filepath)` When a file has been deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:127
msgid "`renamed(newPath, oldPath)` When a file has been renamed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:128
msgid "`end()` When the watcher is closed and watches have been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:129
msgid "`error(err)` When an error occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:130
msgid "`nomatch` When no files have been matched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:132
msgid "Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:134
msgid ""
"`emit(event, [...])` Wrapper for `EventEmitter.emit`. "
"`added`|`changed`|`renamed`|`deleted` events will also trigger the `all` "
"event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:136
msgid "`close()` Unwatch all files and reset the watch instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:137
msgid "`add(patterns, callback)` Adds file(s) `patterns` to be watched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:138
msgid ""
"`remove(filepath)` Removes a file or directory from being watched. Does "
"not recurse directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:140
msgid "`watched()` Returns the currently watched files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:141
msgid ""
"`relative([dir, unixify])` Returns the currently watched files with "
"relative paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:142
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`dir` {string} Only return relative files for this directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:143
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`unixify` {boolean} Return paths with `/` instead of `\\\\` if on Windows."
msgstr ""

