#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:160
msgid "Release History"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:161
msgid ""
"1.1.3 - Fix for Node 10 support (@aredridel). Officially dropping support"
" for Node < 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:162
msgid "1.1.2 - Prevent more `ENOENT` errors from escaping (@alexgorbatchev)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:163
msgid ""
"1.1.1 - Prevent `fs.watch` errors from escaping error handler (@rosen-"
"vladimirov). Fix `_addToWatched` without `path.sep` (@wyicwx)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:164
msgid "1.1.0 - Update to `globule@1.0.0` with `minimatch >= 3.0.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:165
msgid ""
"1.0.0 - Revert back to 0.5.2. Drop support for Node.js v0.8. Fix for "
"`maxListeners`. Update `globule` to `0.2.0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:166
msgid ""
"0.6.4 - Catch and emit `error` from `readdir` (@oconnore). Fix for `0 "
"maxListeners`. Use `graceful-fs` to avoid `EMFILE` errors in other places"
" `fs` is used. Better method to determine if `pathwatcher` was built. Fix"
" keeping process alive too much, only init `pathwatcher` if a file is "
"being watched. Set min required to Windows Vista when building on Windows"
" (@pvolok)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:167
msgid "0.6.3 - Add support for Node.js v0.11"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:168
msgid ""
"0.6.2 - Fix argument error with `watched()`. Fix for erroneous `added` "
"events on folders. Ignore `msvs` build error 4244."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:169
msgid "0.6.1 - Fix for absolute paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:170
msgid ""
"0.6.0 - Uses native OS events (fork of `pathwatcher`) but can fall back "
"to stat polling. Everything is async to avoid blocking, including "
"`relative()` and `watched()`. Better error handling. Update to "
"`globule@0.2.0`. No longer watches `cwd` by default. Added `mode` option."
" Better `EMFILE` message. Avoids `ENOENT` errors with symlinks. All "
"constructor arguments are optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:171
msgid "0.5.2 - Fix for `ENOENT` error with non-existent symlinks [BACKPORTED]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:172
msgid ""
"0.5.1 - Use `setImmediate` (`process.nextTick` for Node.js v0.8) to defer"
" `ready`/`nomatch` events (@amasad)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:173
msgid ""
"0.5.0 - Process is now kept alive while watching files. Emits a `nomatch`"
" event when no files are matching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:174
msgid "0.4.3 - Track file additions in newly created folders (@brett-shwom)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:175
msgid ""
"0.4.2 - Fix `.remove()` method to remove a single file in a directory "
"(@kaelzhang). Fixing “`Cannot call method 'call' of undefined`” "
"(@krasimir). Track new file additions within folders (@brett-shwom)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:176
msgid ""
"0.4.1 - Fix `watchDir` not respecting close in race condition "
"(@chrisirhc)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:177
msgid ""
"0.4.0 - Drop support for Node.js v0.6. Use `globule` for file matching. "
"Avoid Node.js v0.10 `path.resolve`/`join` errors. Register new files when"
" added to non-existent folder. Multiple instances can now poll the same "
"files (@jpommerening)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:178
msgid ""
"0.3.4 - Code clean up. Fix “`path must be strings`” errors (@groner). Fix"
" incorrect `added` events (@groner)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:179
msgid "0.3.3 - Fix for multiple patterns with negate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:180
msgid "0.3.2 - Emit `end` before `removeAllListeners`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:181
msgid "0.3.1 - Fix `added` events within subfolder patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:182
msgid ""
"0.3.0 - Handle safewrite events, `forceWatchMethod` option removed, bug "
"fixes and watch optimizations (@rgaskill)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:183
msgid ""
"0.2.2 - Fix issue where subsequent `add` calls dont get watched "
"(@samcday). `removeAllListeners` on `close`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:184
msgid "0.2.1 - Fix issue with invalid `added` events in current working dir."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:185
msgid ""
"0.2.0 - Support and mark folders with `path.sep`. Add `forceWatchMethod` "
"option. Support `renamed` events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:186
msgid "0.1.6 - Recognize the `cwd` option properly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:187
msgid "0.1.5 - Catch “`too many open file`” errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:188
msgid "0.1.4 - Really fix the race condition with 2 watches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:189
msgid "0.1.3 - Fix race condition with 2 watches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:190
msgid "0.1.2 - Read triggering changed event fix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:191
msgid "0.1.1 - Minor fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/gaze_README.md:192
msgid "0.1.0 - Initial release"
msgstr ""

